		<item>
		<title>The Results From the First LEGO Ideas Review of 2026 Are Here</title>
		<link>https://www.toysnbricks.com/the-results-from-the-first-lego-ideas-review-of-2026-are-here/</link>
					<comments>https://www.toysnbricks.com/the-results-from-the-first-lego-ideas-review-of-2026-are-here/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[News Reporter]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:11:19 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[18+/Hard to Find Theme]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Editor's Picks]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[General]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Ideas Creations]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[IDEAS Theme]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[LEGO Creations]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[LEGO News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Themes]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.toysnbricks.com/?p=114555</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="2000" height="1333" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured.jpg" class="attachment-post-thumbnail size-post-thumbnail wp-post-image" alt="lego ideas results nov 2026 featured" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured.jpg 2000w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-1536x1024.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px" /></p>
<p>In a highly-anticipated announcement, LEGO (USA &#124; Canada &#124; UK &#124; Australia) has finally revealed the results from its</p>
<p>© Toys N Bricks: 2009-Present. <a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com/the-results-from-the-first-lego-ideas-review-of-2026-are-here/">The Results From the First LEGO Ideas Review of 2026 Are Here</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com"></a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>In a highly-anticipated announcement, LEGO (<a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=13923&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-us%2Fcategories%2Fnew-sets-and-products" target="_blank" rel="noopener">USA</a> | <a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=36166&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-ca%2Fcategories%2Fnew-sets-and-products" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Canada</a> | <a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=24340&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-gb%2Fcategories%2Fnew-sets-and-products" target="_blank" rel="noopener">UK</a> | <a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=46079&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-au%2Fcategories%2Fnew-sets-and-products" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Australia</a>) has finally revealed the results from its first LEGO Ideas Review of 2026. For those unfamiliar, LEGO Ideas is a platform where fans can submit their own custom designs for potential LEGO sets. If a design gets 10,000 votes from supporters, it reaches the review stage, where LEGO evaluates it and chooses to either approve or deny the design.</p>
<p>Ahead of this recent announcement, 97 Product Ideas had reached the review stage during this period. Of these designs, only three were approved, while two were added to the Parking Lot, which is LEGO&#8217;s holding category for ideas that need an extended review.</p>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class=" wp-image-114556 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured.jpg" alt="" width="1299" height="866" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured.jpg 2000w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/lego-ideas-nov-2026-featured-1536x1024.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1299px) 100vw, 1299px" /></p>
<p>The three approved designs that have been chosen to move into development include:</p>
<ul>
<li>Chinese Cork Carving Art by GenericBrix</li>
<li>Interstellar by Minibrick41587</li>
<li>Tulip Field Windmill by HisBrickMaterials</li>
</ul>
<p>Let&#8217;s take a closer look at each of these designs.</p>
<p>Don&#8217;t miss out on any LEGO Deals or News by subscribing to our email list!</p>
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Bookmark Toysnbricks.com and be sure to subscribe to the <a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com/email-subscription/" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener" data-cke-saved-href="https://www.toysnbricks.com/email-subscription/">free Toysnbricks newsletter subscription</a>. You’ll get a choice of daily LEGO News, LEGO Sales &amp; Deals or All Updates right in your inbox. Alternatively, you can also <a href="https://www.toysnbricks.com/rss-feed-lego-updates/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">follow us on our RSS Feeds</a> with your RSS Reader/App to get timely updates.</p>
<h2>Chinese Cork Carving Art by GenericBrix</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-114559" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-cork-carving-art.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1333" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-cork-carving-art.jpg 2000w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-cork-carving-art-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-cork-carving-art-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-cork-carving-art-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/chinese-cork-carving-art-1536x1024.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px" /></p>
<p>This is a stunning set that&#8217;s inspired by traditional cork carvings, and uses several warm, woody, and earth tones to mimic the look and feel of cork well. From the temples, to the trees, to the landscape, there are plenty of details that catch your eye when viewing this piece.</p>
<h2>Interstellar by Minibrick41587</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-114560" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/interstellar.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1334" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/interstellar.jpg 2000w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/interstellar-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/interstellar-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/interstellar-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/interstellar-1536x1025.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px" /></p>
<p>This set is inspired by the Oscar-winning film, Interstellar, and features mini figures of both Dr. Brand and Cooper, as well as the TARS and CASE robots. However, the star of the show is the famous Ranger spaceship, which features a fully-decorated interior space and plenty of accessories.</p>
<h2>Tulip Field Windmill by HisBrickMaterials</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-114561" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tulip-field-windmill.jpg" alt="" width="1896" height="1264" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tulip-field-windmill.jpg 1896w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tulip-field-windmill-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tulip-field-windmill-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tulip-field-windmill-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/tulip-field-windmill-1536x1024.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1896px) 100vw, 1896px" /></p>
<p>According to the creator, this stunning set is inspired by the landscapes of the Netherlands. It&#8217;s fully of beautiful details, ranging fron the vibrant colors at the base to the classic windmill that actually rotates. But in addition to the exterior, the inside of this set also has plenty to offer, as there&#8217;s a fully-furnished interior that includes a staircase, bedroom, kitchen, and more.</p>
<p>In addition to these three approved designs, the two designs that were added to the Parking Lot are The 5th Element – Korben Dallas Taxi by MarinBrickDesign and Peashooter by DistinguishedCrow.</p>
<h2>The 5th Element – Korben Dallas Taxi by MarinBrickDesign</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-114558" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/korben-dallas-taxi.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1333" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/korben-dallas-taxi.jpg 2000w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/korben-dallas-taxi-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/korben-dallas-taxi-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/korben-dallas-taxi-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/korben-dallas-taxi-1536x1024.jpg 1536w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 2000px) 100vw, 2000px" /></p>
<p>This set highlights Korben Dallas&#8217;s flying taxi from the 1997 hit film, The 5th Element. In addition to looking great on its own as a display piece, you can also open the taxi up and reveal a detailed interior that features the equipment seen in the movie. It also has mini figures of both Korben Dallas and Leeloo.</p>
<h2>Peashooter by DistinguishedCrow</h2>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-114557" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/peashooter.jpg" alt="" width="1080" height="720" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/peashooter.jpg 1080w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/peashooter-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/peashooter-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/peashooter-768x512.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1080px) 100vw, 1080px" /></p>
<p>A reference to the iconic character from the Plants vs Zombies games, the Peashooter set features posable leaves at the base, comes with a pea so you can display it while it shoots, and was designed by the creator to be smooth and as game-accurate as possible.</p>
<p>&#8212;</p>
<p>For the most up to date current LEGO promotions, offers and gift with purchase (GWP) being offered, check the official LEGO store promotional pages links below.</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=13923&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-us%2Fpage%2Flego-offers-promotions" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>US United States</strong> – LEGO Shop at Home Promotional Offers Page</a></li>
<li><a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=36166&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-ca%2Fpage%2Flego-offers-promotions" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Canada</strong> – LEGO Shop at Home Promotional Offers Page</a></li>
<li><a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=24340&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-gb%2Fpage%2Flego-offers-promotions" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>UK United Kingdom</strong> – LEGO Shop at Home Promotional Offers Page</a></li>
<li><a href="https://click.linksynergy.com/deeplink?id=R/1WEHEfGiI&amp;mid=46079&amp;murl=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.lego.com%2Fen-au%2Fpage%2Flego-offers-promotions" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><strong>Australia</strong> – LEGO Shop at Home Promotional Offers Page</a></li>
</ul>
<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="size-full wp-image-103542 aligncenter" src="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/LEGO-Sales-Deals-Logo-Banner-Discount-Savings.jpg" alt="" width="909" height="459" srcset="https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/LEGO-Sales-Deals-Logo-Banner-Discount-Savings.jpg 909w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/LEGO-Sales-Deals-Logo-Banner-Discount-Savings-300x151.jpg 300w, https://www.toysnbricks.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/LEGO-Sales-Deals-Logo-Banner-Discount-Savings-768x388.jpg 768w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 909px) 100vw, 909px" /></p>
